# Lab 1 – Getting Started with GitHub

## Objective

The objective of this lab was to become familiar with GitHub by creating my first public repository, uploading files, and learning how GitHub will be used throughout the course to manage and showcase machine learning projects.

## What I Did

In this lab, I created a GitHub account, set up my first public repository, and uploaded my first project file. I also learned how to commit changes and submit a repository link for review. This assignment served as an introduction to version control and repository management.

## What I Learned

This lab introduced me to GitHub and helped me understand its role in organizing projects, tracking changes, and sharing work with others. I learned the basics of creating repositories, uploading files, and using GitHub as a professional portfolio for future machine learning projects.

## Skills & Tools

* GitHub
* Repository creation
* File uploads
* Version control basics
* Repository organization

